{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"113613","commit":"9b323fb20a5886715faa880017bf0ce7cccff28f","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `adjustBreaker` method in `MemoryTrackingTDigestArrays` and `DelegatingTDigestArrays` now correctly adjusts the circuit breaker based on the size parameter. Verify that this change does not lead to incorrect memory accounting and that all places using these arrays properly adjust the breaker.","nodes":[{"id":"libs/tdigest/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/TDigestTestCase.java-libs/tdigest/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/TDigestTestCase.java--3249:3357","promptId":"#N90P5","srcPath":"libs/tdigest/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/TDigestTestCase.java","dstPath":"libs/tdigest/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/TDigestTestCase.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3249,"endPos":3357,"startLine":85,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":88,"endLineOffset":9,"length":109}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/MemoryTrackingTDigestArrays.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/MemoryTrackingTDigestArrays.java--1404:1642","promptId":"#2YP2D","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/MemoryTrackingTDigestArrays.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/aggregations/metrics/MemoryTrackingTDigestArrays.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1404,"endPos":1642,"startLine":37,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":44,"endLineOffset":5,"length":239}]}]},{"comment":"The `close` method in several classes (e.g., `MergingDigest`, `SortingDigest`, `TDigestState`) now checks if the object is already closed before proceeding with cleanup. This prevents double-closing and ensures that resources are only released once. However, it\u0027s important to ensure that all methods modifying the state of these objects properly check the `closed` flag to avoid concurrent modification issues. The `centroidCount` method in `MergingDigest` now merges new values before counting centroids. This ensures that the count reflects the most up-to-date state of the digest. Verify that this change does not introduce performance issues, especially for large datasets. The `ramBytesUsed` method in `TDigestState` now returns the shallow size of the instance plus the memory used by the underlying TDigest. This ensures that memory usage is accurately tracked. Verify that this change does not lead to incorrect memory accounting and that all places using these methods properly adjust the breaker. The `read` method in `TDigestState` now adds an estimate to the circuit breaker before reading a new instance. This ensures that memory usage is tracked accurately. Verify that this change does not lead to incorrect memory accounting and that all places using these methods properly adjust the breaker. The `SortingDigest` class now includes a shallow size constant, an arrays field, and a closed flag. The `close` method now adjusts the circuit breaker before releasing resources. Ensure that this change does not lead to incorrect memory accounting and that all places using these methods properly release resources.","nodes":[{"id":"libs/tdigest/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigestTests.java-libs/tdigest/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigestTests.java-1460:1561,1571:1588,1597:1641,1650:1793,1803:1852,1861:1898,1907:2143,2152:2174,2184:2223,2232:2303,2312:2364,2374:2698-1505:2918","promptId":"#ARCM3","srcPath":"libs/tdigest/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigestTests.java","dstPath":"libs/tdigest/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigestTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":1460,"endPos":1561,"startLine":43,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":43,"endLineOffset":109,"length":102},{"pos":1571,"endPos":1588,"startLine":45,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":45,"endLineOffset":25,"length":18},{"pos":1597,"endPos":1641,"startLine":46,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine"